commit fd218ac887ba0e1e46b160323262d04d8450dd57
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 09:58:05 2026 +1100

    db: Import the DB API inside the functions using it
    
    neutron.common.utils, neutron.service and neutron.api.api_common import
    neutron_lib.db.api or model_base for one function each, and every agent
    imports them. Import them in those functions, and test in a fresh
    interpreter that the modules neither refer to nor load the DB API.
    
    This saves nothing alone. With "ovn: Keep server-only imports out of
    the OVN agent" and "agent: Import the resource cache only for L2
    agents", the probe shows the OVN, DHCP, L3 and metadata agents 4 to
    12MB smaller; with neutron-lib's "Load the DB API only for DB users" as
    well, 10 to 17MB smaller and without the DB API or pecan. The load test
    is skipped until neutron-lib stops loading the DB API.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for the neutron changes that keep the DB API out of
    the neutron agents, as three patches grouped by the agents they free.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    
    Depends-On: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/devstack/+/1011992
    Change-Id: I8ac2f724332dce3346ea92ec927be125083562ed
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

